From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:11:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 340/342] meson_gpio: the LCD shield's D5 and D7 were on each
 other's pins

D5 is header pin 26 and D7 pin 36 (Hardkernel's example drives the LEDs
on wiringPi 21, 22, 23, 24, 11, 26, 27); the table had them the other way
round, so "0000100" lit D7. The swap was seen on a real shield.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/misc/meson_gpio/lcd_shield.cpp | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/misc/meson_gpio/lcd_shield.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/misc/meson_gpio/lcd_shield.cpp
index c0d1e3ebcb..3791a4ae35 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/misc/meson_gpio/lcd_shield.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/misc/meson_gpio/lcd_shield.cpp
@@ -12,8 +12,9 @@
  *     E 11, D4 13, D5 15, D6 12, D7 16; its R/W is tied low, so it is only
  *     written, and its busy flag can't be read: commands get the
  *     datasheet's time instead (37 us, 1.52 ms to clear or go home);
- *   - LEDs D1 to D7 on pins 29, 31, 33, 35, 36, 32, 26, each through
- *     3.9 kOhm to ground: high is lit;
+ *   - LEDs D1 to D7 on pins 29, 31, 33, 35, 26, 32, 36, each through
+ *     3.9 kOhm to ground: high is lit (Hardkernel's example drives them on
+ *     wiringPi 21, 22, 23, 24, 11, 26, 27: D5 is pin 26, D7 pin 36);
  *   - SW1 on pin 18, SW2 on pin 22, closing to ground, with no resistor:
  *     the pins' pull-ups are turned on.
  *
@@ -50,7 +51,7 @@ static const uint32 kRS = 1 << 0;
 static const uint32 kE = 1 << 1;
 static const uint32 kDataShift = 2;
 
-static const uint8 kLedPins[] = { 29, 31, 33, 35, 36, 32, 26 };
+static const uint8 kLedPins[] = { 29, 31, 33, 35, 26, 32, 36 };
 static const uint8 kButtonPins[] = { 18, 22 };
 
 static const bigtime_t kButtonPeriod = 10000;
